WEBVTT

q0001
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.224
How can a kernel be faster while the easy public call is slower?

q0002
00:00:08.224 --> 00:00:19.287
This episode has one job: A timing claim is meaningful only after every included and excluded stage is placed on a common pipeline.

q0003
00:00:19.287 --> 00:00:30.350
We build on From DAGs to flat instructions: operations, storage, and execution; their definitions stay fixed while this lesson adds a new layer.

q0004
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:36.804
A measurement boundary specifies exactly which stages the timer includes.

q0005
00:00:36.804 --> 00:00:45.618
Watch for the label preparation; it stays attached to the artifact this episode means.

q0006
00:00:45.618 --> 00:00:54.432
When we say evaluator kernel, the highlight identifies its layer before we interpret it.

q0007
00:00:54.432 --> 00:01:05.016
The term public wrapper receives its own visual state so it cannot drift into a neighboring concept.

q0008
00:01:05.016 --> 00:01:12.650
We will keep end-to-end task visible whenever its definition controls the inference.

q0009
00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:23.234
The next sequence uses Shared Boolean expression as a conceptual teaching example, not as measured benchmark evidence.

q0010
00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:27.917
Our stable example is Shared Boolean expression.

q0011
00:01:27.917 --> 00:01:38.980
S=A AND B; F=(S AND C AND D) OR (S AND E), with binary source syntax and stable variable order A,B,C,D,E.

q0012
00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:46.024
Carry AST, CSE, CSE-flat, CM-IR, lowering, and operation accounting across episodes.

q0013
00:01:46.024 --> 00:01:54.838
We now construct the Shared Boolean expression and name every part before interpreting it.

q0014
00:01:54.838 --> 00:02:05.422
The accompanying view makes this step concrete: One persistent horizontal pipeline replaces separate cards for every boundary.

q0015
00:02:05.422 --> 00:02:14.826
Move one request through preparation, artifact construction, repeated kernel, wrapper, extraction, persistence, and task completion.

q0016
00:02:14.826 --> 00:02:24.230
Slide timing brackets over different stage subsets and change the allowed claim wording in lockstep.

q0017
00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:33.634
Now isolate preparation, kernel, wrapper, extraction, persistence, and end-to-end timing boundaries inside Shared Boolean expression.

q0018
00:02:33.634 --> 00:02:44.697
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for preparation, kernel, wrapper, extraction, persistence, and end-to-end timing boundaries changes.

q0019
00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:55.760
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to preparation, kernel, wrapper, extraction, persistence, and end-to-end timing boundaries, not to a substituted workload.

q0020
00:02:55.760 --> 00:03:02.214
Colored brackets expand from kernel-only to wrapper and end-to-end scopes.

q0021
00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:13.277
On the exactly counterbalanced B2/B4 V3 workload, formula-balanced bare CM/CSE-flat was 0.8906 with a formula-cluster 95% interval [0.8741, 0.9073].

q0022
00:03:13.277 --> 00:03:22.681
Read that statement only within this scope: B2/B4 V3 formulas on one Windows run.

q0023
00:03:22.681 --> 00:03:29.135
Its declared measurement boundary is compiled evaluator kernel after compilation.

q0024
00:03:29.135 --> 00:03:37.359
The uncertainty field says formula-cluster bootstrap; does not model between-run or between-machine variation.

q0025
00:03:37.359 --> 00:03:44.993
The public CM wrapper was slower than CSE-flat in the corrected comparison.

q0026
00:03:44.993 --> 00:03:52.037
Read that statement only within this scope: corrected B2/B4 comparison.

q0027
00:03:52.037 --> 00:03:58.491
Its declared measurement boundary is public wrapper complete truth-output call.

q0028
00:03:58.491 --> 00:04:05.535
The uncertainty field says local formula-cluster interval plus descriptive pod replication.

q0029
00:04:05.535 --> 00:04:16.598
EPFL CM preparation was 4.11x CSE-flat preparation; 55 of 129 cases never broke even under the retained calculation.

q0030
00:04:16.598 --> 00:04:23.052
Read that statement only within this scope: accepted EPFL workload.

q0031
00:04:23.052 --> 00:04:29.506
Its declared measurement boundary is preparation and modeled reuse break-even.

q0032
00:04:29.506 --> 00:04:34.189
The uncertainty field says descriptive retained calculation.

q0033
00:04:34.189 --> 00:04:41.823
Current evidence does not support a universal claim that CM beats CSE-flat.

q0034
00:04:41.823 --> 00:04:47.687
Read that statement only within this scope: cross-study synthesis.

q0035
00:04:47.687 --> 00:04:53.551
Its declared measurement boundary is multiple boundaries kept separate.

q0036
00:04:53.551 --> 00:04:59.415
The uncertainty field says scopes are intentionally not pooled.

q0037
00:04:59.415 --> 00:05:10.478
The nearest confusing lesson is How to read a CM/comparator ratio; it owns ratio direction, while this episode owns preparation, kernel, wrapper, extraction, persistence, and end-to-end timing boundaries.

q0038
00:05:10.478 --> 00:05:21.541
Begin with A and B, compute the shared subexpression S once, and keep that identity color on every outgoing use.

q0039
00:05:21.541 --> 00:05:32.125
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate preparation, kernel, wrapper, extraction, persistence, and end-to-end timing boundaries.

q0040
00:05:32.125 --> 00:05:43.188
The left branch combines S with C and D, while the right branch combines the same S with E.

q0041
00:05:43.188 --> 00:05:54.251
Both branches meet at the final OR, so the shared node changes program structure without changing the Boolean output.

q0042
00:05:54.251 --> 00:06:05.314
A raw syntax view may draw S twice; a shared graph draws one node with two outgoing edges.

q0043
00:06:05.314 --> 00:06:14.128
Lowering the graph assigns dependency-ordered slots, but slot numbers are not new Boolean operations.

q0044
00:06:14.128 --> 00:06:22.942
Instruction count, primitive execution count, live buffers, and packed storage therefore remain separate ledgers.

q0045
00:06:22.942 --> 00:06:34.005
Changing from bigint bits to word lanes changes storage and execution layout, not the meaning of S or F.

q0046
00:06:34.005 --> 00:06:44.589
The stable variable order A through E prevents a convenient reordering from hiding inside a method comparison.

q0047
00:06:44.589 --> 00:06:55.173
Any claimed reduction must point to the repeated S path or another named transformation actually present here.

q0048
00:06:55.173 --> 00:07:05.167
The output check closes both paths against the same exact truth behavior before performance is interpreted.

q0049
00:07:05.167 --> 00:07:16.230
The starting state preserves the stable definition: S=A AND B; F=(S AND C AND D) OR (S AND E), with binary source syntax and stable variable order A,B,C,D,E.

q0050
00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:27.293
After the change, the composition makes preparation, kernel, wrapper, extraction, persistence, and end-to-end timing boundaries inspectable: Colored brackets expand from kernel-only to wrapper and end-to-end scopes.

q0051
